> 1) Did you learn any Lojban vocabulary so far?

Yes.

> If you said =93no=94, the survey is done for you. If you said =93yes=94, =
go on:
> 2) How many of the gismu do you have memorized right now?

Well over a thousand. About 1100-1200.

> 3) How many rafsi?

I never counted them, but I know a large number. I never used a specific=20
tool to learn them, but learned them by making lots of lujvo.

> 4) And how many cmavo?

99%

(+ 99% of the experimental cmavo)

> 5) When did you start learning vocabulary?

The moment I heard the first word of Lojban. (no flashcards, just exposure)

> 6) How often (roughly) do (or did) you learn?

I don't sit down and learn words in isolation. I use the language and=20
that's how the words become familiar on a personal level.

> 7) On a regular basis?

I don't use tools, but I do use the language every single day of my=20
life, and I consider that the best practice one can get.

> 8) Which learning tool or learning method do you use?

There was a short period in which I used memrise, but on the whole it's=20
not my preferred way of learning vocabulary. I learned a lot by=20
conversing on IRC and by translating massive amounts of text into=20
Lojban. I would also recommend *reading* texts to everyone. It's so much=20
more effective than flashcards in my opinion. But to each their own.

mu'o mi'e la selpa'i

